💡 **SUGGESTION: untyped `calendar` parameter (implicit `dynamic`) — re-raised from the previous round**

Both helpers still declare the parameter untyped:

```dart
Future<bool> _calendarReady(calendar) async { ... }
Future<void> _fetchUpcomingEvents(calendar) async { ... }
```

The bare identifier defaults to `dynamic`, which compiles under this repo's lints but weakens static checking and deviates from the surrounding style where every parameter carries a type. The concrete type is `CalendarApi` (the `createCalendarService()` return type, see `lib/services/calendar_service_io.dart:15`), so this is a one-word fix at both sites:

```dart
Future<bool> _calendarReady(CalendarApi calendar) async { ... }
Future<void> _fetchUpcomingEvents(CalendarApi calendar) async { ... }
```

